; C1b-nontop and C1b-top  Winning 42 pp. 37-38 (W42-p037-h, W42-p038-c,
; W42-p038-d; played in Hands 31 and 32, pp. 106, 109)
; Rule, in our words: the bidder's partner, out of trump, follows the bidder's
; trump lead. If the lead is the highest trump still unplayed, the trick is
; safe: give count, the biggest first. If a live trump can still beat the lead,
; the trick is not safe: give no count.
; Python gate (pour_bidder gate_c1b): the same two branches. The two gate ids
; are one rule with two branches, so they share this file.
; How this encoding differs: the "top" branch is the else of the "not top"
; branch (negation by rule order). If the lead is not the top trump and every
; tile the partner holds is count, the not-top rule selects nothing and the top
; rules give the largest count; the gate does not fire there.
; Out of trump is read from the hand: following a trump lead, a legal tile that
; is not trump proves the viewer holds no trump.
; GAP declarer: the bidder is written in as S0, the partner as S2.
; GAP none: "the lead is the top trump" is "no live tile beats it", a negated
; existential; Silas negates single atoms only.
(policy c01b-partner-count-on-a-trump-lead
  (initial play)
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule not-top-lead-no-count (in play) (next play) (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (domino give) (domino led) (domino over))
        (out give)
        (pattern
          (viewer S2)
          (leader S0)
          (led-context q*)
          (trick-play S0 led)
          (live over)
          (beats over led q*)
          (own-legal give)
          (not (in give q*))
          (count give 0)))))
  ; GAP none: the two rules below hold only because the rule above did not select.
  (rule top-lead-give-ten (in play) (next play) (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (domino give))
        (out give)
        (pattern
          (viewer S2)
          (leader S0)
          (led-context q*)
          (own-legal give)
          (not (in give q*))
          (count give 10)))))
  (rule top-lead-give-five (in play) (next play) (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (domino give))
        (out give)
        (pattern
          (viewer S2)
          (leader S0)
          (led-context q*)
          (own-legal give)
          (not (in give q*))
          (count give 5))))))
